  How to calculate when there are many if, else statements inside loops? As discussed here, the worst-case time complexity is the most useful among best, average and worst. Therefore we need to consider the worst case. We evaluate the situation when values in if-else conditions cause a maximum number of statements to be executed. For example, consider the linear search function where we consider the case when an element is present at the end or not present at all. When the code is too complex to consider all if-else cases, we can get an upper bound by ignoring if-else and other complex control statements.
